---
import Article from "../layouts/Article.astro";
import { experiments } from "../data/charts";
---

<Article
  title="llmango"
  description="Measuring how much genuine randomness an LLM has under a forced choice, and how that choice shifts with language."
>
  <h1>llmango</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    How much genuine randomness does a language model have under a forced choice,
    and how much does that choice shift with the language you ask in?
  </p>
  <p>
    One question, asked across several languages and schema variants, thousands of
    samples each, then aggregated into distributions. Every run is pinned to a
    manifest, every raw response is kept, and every chart on this site is drawn by
    the same pipeline that produced the numbers.
  </p>

  <h2>Experiments</h2>
  <ul class="listing">
    <li>
      <a href="/001-fruit">001 &mdash; fruit</a>
      <p>
        Pick one fruit from a list. Four questions vary option order, prompt
        language and response schema, one at a time.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p class="meta">
    {experiments.length} experiment{experiments.length === 1 ? "" : "s"} charted.
    Raw responses ship as an open dataset; aggregates and charts are committed to
    the repository.
  </p>
</Article>
